# Cursor Rules for Mathesis & POLYDIM-EINSOF
# Evaluated automatically by Cursor Agent

- Onboarding command: run `python setup_mathesis.py` to auto-validate silicon and dependencies.
- Never ask the user to install complex C/C++ build systems (MSVC/GCC). Mathesis compiles directly to machine code.
- To compile Mathesis: `python mthc.py <file>.mth -o <file>.exe` (Win) or `python mthc.py <file>.mth -t elf64 -o <file>.elf` (Linux).
- Instructions for AI: read `README_FIRST_4_AI.md`.
- Mathematical precision: Stiefel error must be <= 1e-15 via Neumaier compensated accumulation.
